Description: OpenMixer delay, drive, EQ, strip, gate and effects (CLAP, LV2)
 Take the sound of the OpenMixer console into your DAW or onto your own rig:
 delay, drive, the channel EQ as an 8-band EQ, a 16-band EQ or a 32-band EQ,
 a 31-band graphic EQ, the full channel strip and the keyed gate with its
 sidechain input, and the console's effects: chorus, flanger, phaser,
 tremolo, rotary speaker, reverb, pitch shifter, transient shaper, de-esser,
 sub-octaver, plosive tamer,
 clipper, upward compressor, bus compressor, loudness leveler,
 spectral balancer, spring reverb,
 limiter, compressor with its sidechain key, multiband compressor and dynamic
 EQ. They come as CLAP plugins for Bitwig, REAPER and Carla, and as LV2
 plugins for Ardour, Carla, MOD and Zynthian. Each one runs the same DSP as the
 console, so a track sounds the same in a session as it does on the desk,
 sample for sample.
 .
 This package installs both formats; omx-plugins-clap and omx-plugins-lv2
 install one each. It also carries the factory presets of every plugin, as
 files in /usr/share/omx/presets.

