Homepage: https://github.com/FreeMixer/plugin-hostd
Description: run LV2 and CLAP plugins so that one crash cannot stop the show
 plugin-hostd keeps your effects and instruments running when one of them
 misbehaves. It gives a controller one mod-host socket and starts each plugin,
 or each named group of plugins, in a worker process of its own: omx-clap-host
 for CLAP and, through its LV2 adapter, for LV2. If a plugin crashes, only its
 worker goes down and the daemon brings it back. Audio never passes through the
 daemon, so it adds no latency: every worker is a JACK client.
 .
 A format whose worker is not installed refuses its adds; the other formats
 are unaffected. mod-host runs LV2 plugins only when you ask for it.
 .
 Its documentation is on openmixer.org.

